From 855ebe9a17bd4d44904f811dbe7c26b71a66c2c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 04:25:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] swscale/ppc: add AltiVec scaler-path packed 4:2:2 packers

Add yuv2packed1/2/X AltiVec kernels for yuyv422/yvyu422/uyvy422 to
libswscale/ppc/yuv2yuv_altivec.c, registered from a new
ff_sws_init_yuv2packed422_ppc() entry point called by
ff_sws_init_swscale_ppc(). This is the general scaler's packed-output
path (libswscale/output.c's yuv2422_{1,2,X}_c_template), distinct from
the unscaled planar->packed converters already in this file.

Design, verified in the new file comment: the C references only clip
(and only then match true 8-bit saturation) when the pre-clip int is in
[-256, 511]; outside that window they store the low byte of an
unclamped value that nothing sane depends on. Every AltiVec step that
could overflow uses a genuinely saturating op (vec_adds for the _1
luma/chroma "+64" step, vec_packs/vec_packsu for the final narrowing),
so the kernels equal the C reference everywhere the reference is
well-defined -- hence no SWS_BITEXACT/SWS_FULL_CHR_H_INT/needAlpha gate
on registration, exactly mirroring the C dispatch
(output.c:3800-3813). One av_always_inline template per variant (_1,
_2, _X) takes the target format as a compile-time-constant parameter,
each with 3 thin wrappers, following the existing
planar_to_packed422_altivec/output.c pattern.

Per call: pairs = (dstW+1)>>1, an 8-pairs-per-iteration vector loop
(16 luma + 8 chroma samples -> 32 output bytes via two store16 calls),
then a scalar tail that is the C body verbatim including the "& 0x100"
clip idiom. Byte assembly reuses the sub-task-1 kernel's proven order:
pack luma to u8 (already Y1,Y2,... order, since that is simply buf0's
own element order), pack U,V together, interleave via vec_sld+vec_mergeh
into u0,v0,u1,v1,... (or v-first for YVYU), then interleave with luma in
the target's byte order. _1's chroma branches once per call on
uvalpha < 2048 (mirroring the C); _2's per-line blend coefficients and
_X's per-tap accumulation both use the vec_mule/vec_mulo + mergeh/mergel
"restore order" idiom already used by yuv2planeX_8 in swscale_altivec.c
for the same reason (no mixed even/odd multiply on classic AltiVec).

Validated with tests/checkasm/sw_yuv2yuv.c's new check_yuv2packed422_1/2/X
(previous commit): seeds 1, 42, 777, 5, 99 all pass; --bench --duration=100
lists _altivec rows for all 9 (format x variant) names (45 individual
parameter rows) alongside the still-present sub-task-1 names. Both
touched files were also compiled standalone in the plain and
-D_ARCH_PWR4 shapes with -Wall -Wextra: no new warnings (the few
warnings present pre-exist in code this patch does not touch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xix7Wn4UbWrKRBNAMUVpRR
---
 libswscale/ppc/swscale_altivec.c |   2 +
 libswscale/ppc/yuv2yuv_altivec.c | 417 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libswscale/swscale_internal.h    |   9 +
 3 files changed, 428 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libswscale/ppc/swscale_altivec.c b/libswscale/ppc/swscale_altivec.c
index 3112c6c..2a26dac 100644
--- a/libswscale/ppc/swscale_altivec.c
+++ b/libswscale/ppc/swscale_altivec.c
@@ -238,6 +238,8 @@ av_cold void ff_sws_init_swscale_ppc(SwsInternal *c)
     if (!(av_get_cpu_flags() & AV_CPU_FLAG_ALTIVEC))
         return;
 
+    ff_sws_init_yuv2packed422_ppc(c);
